  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Keep your tail",
  "description": "Mark an area across the ice with a middle zone of cones. Everyone has a stick, a ball and a bib as a tail, tucked loosely into the back of their trousers so it comes out at a light tug. A hunter (red) stands in the middle zone. The hunter leaves their stick by the boards and hunts with free hands, so there is no stick near the other players’ legs.\n\nThe players take the ball through the middle zone to the other side, and back again. The hunter must stay in the middle zone and tries to grab the tails as the players skate past – only the tail, never holding on, pushing or touching the stick. Each player counts how many times they get through with their tail on. Anyone who loses their tail fetches it and tucks it back in. Change hunter often. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Look up before you skate into the zone – where is the hunter?"
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Change direction and speed with your edges to get past."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Turn your body so the tail is away from the hunter, and keep the ball on the other side."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "The hunter only pulls the tail. It should come out easily so nobody loses their balance and falls."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
